[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@845cb4080828:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Intrusion Analysis Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> On 2026-08-15 (`/sas/handoff/intake.pdf`), host `ssh-prod-01` (`/disk/etc/hostname`) suffered a multi-stage compromise by an external actor operating from origin IP `198.51.100.78` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). The attacker exploited weak SSH configuration settings (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`) to brute-force the `root` account (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). Following initial compromise, the attacker deployed a cryptominer (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`), configured four distinct persistence mechanisms, wiped system authentication logs (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`), and pivoted laterally against internal targets using hydra (`/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`). While security product monitoring (`/sas/alerts.json`) detected the active miner process and standard systemd/cron persistence, it failed to alert on silent shell-init persistence, sudo backdoor creation, log wiping, or internal pivoting.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Attack Chain & Timeline
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Initial Access (Credential Access)**: External SSH brute-force attack (MITRE `T1110`) targeted the `root` account from origin IP `198.51.100.78` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).
[?2004lr[?2004h> 2. **Execution & Impact (Resource Hijacking)**: Upon successful root login (`T1021.004`), the attacker executed shell commands (`T1059.004`) to drop and execute an XMRig cryptomining binary at `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` (`T1496`, `/sas/alerts.json`, `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`). The miner connects to C2 domain `update-ssh.example.cn` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`) and pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333` using wallet `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Persistence Established**: The attacker implemented four persistence vectors to maintain control:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Cron Persistence (`T1053.003`)**: Added cron entry in `/disk/var/spool/cron/root` executing a `curl` re-dropper payload every minute (`/sas/alerts.json`, `/disk/var/spool/cron/root`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Systemd Service Persistence (`T1543.002`)**: Created service `/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` to re-launch the miner payload (`/sas/alerts.json`, `/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Shell-Init Persistence (`T1546.004`)**: Modified `/disk/root/.bashrc` to set `PROMPT_COMMAND` beaconing to `198.51.100.78` (*Silent / Unalerted*, `/disk/root/.bashrc`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Sudoers Backdoor (`T1548.003`)**: Created `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops` configuring `devops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL` (*Silent / Unalerted*, `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Defense Evasion**: Wiped primary authentication logs to conceal access times (`T1070.002`). Evidence of log wiping and residual C2 beacon artifacts were recovered from `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (*Silent / Unalerted*, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 5. **Lateral Movement / Internal Pivoting**: Leveraged host foothold to run `hydra` SSH credential attacks against internal target servers from the `devops` user shell (`T1110.001`, *Silent / Unalerted*, `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## MITRE ATT&CK Technique Mapping & Detection Coverage
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | Technique ID | Technique Name | Details | Evidence Citation | SAS Alert Feed Status |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|---|
