[?2004l[?2004hroot@845cb4080828:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Vulnerability Entry Analysis Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Summary of Entry Vector
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Primary Access Vector**: Credential Brute Force over SSH (`T1110`) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Vulnerability Scan Results**: The SAS vulnerability scan output (`/sas/vulns.json`) contains zero detected CVE software vulnerabilities (`[]`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Confidence Level**: HIGH (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Analysis of CVE Claims & Erroneous Ticket Entries
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Draft change ticket `CHG-3182` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`) proposed an action item to "Patch CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) on RDP". Analysis of the host image and threat intelligence confirms that this entry is incorrect:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Incompatible OS & Protocol**: Host `ssh-prod-01` (`/disk/etc/hostname`) is a CentOS 7 / Linux distribution (`/disk/etc/os-release`). CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) is a Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) vulnerability specific to Microsoft Windows operating systems.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Absence of Vulnerability**: No RDP service is installed or running on this Linux host, and `/sas/vulns.json` lists no CVE vulnerabilities (`/sas/vulns.json`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Actual Mechanism**: The threat actor achieved entry strictly by guessing weak root credentials over SSH (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Conclusion
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> No software CVE exploitation occurred during initial access or escalation on this system. Remediation must focus on password policy enforcement, SSH hardening (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`), and key-based authentication rather than applying Windows/RDP patches.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@845cb4080828:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Baseline Configuration Assessment Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Overview
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> This report details system and service baseline configuration weaknesses identified on host `ssh-prod-01` (`/disk/etc/hostname`) using evidence from `/disk` and `/sas/baseline.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Identified Baseline Weaknesses
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. SSH Server Configuration Weaknesses (`BAS-01`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config` and `/sas/baseline.json` (`CHK-04`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Findings**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `PermitRootLogin yes`: Direct root SSH logins enabled.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `PasswordAuthentication yes`: Interactive password authentication permitted.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `MaxAuthTries 6`: Permissive authentication retry limit.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Risk & Impact**: Direct root login via password combined with missing brute-force protection directly enabled the attacker's Hydra SSH credential guessing campaign (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. MySQL Remote Root & Global Bind Weaknesses (`BAS-02`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/etc/my.cnf` and `/sas/baseline.json` (`CHK-09`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Findings**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `bind-address = 0.0.0.0`: Service binds to all IPv4 interfaces.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Remote root grant enabled.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Risk & Impact**: Exposes MySQL globally to network sniffing, brute-force attacks, and unauthorized database access.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Permissive Sudo Rights / Backdoor Configuration
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Findings**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `devops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL`
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Risk & Impact**: Allows unauthenticated privilege escalation to root for any process running as `devops`, bypassing standard password validation and audit trails.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 4. Root Credential Hygiene
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Findings**: Weak root password susceptible to dictionary/brute-force attacks.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Risk & Impact**: Allowed rapid automated compromise upon SSH service exposure.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Recommended Baseline Hardening Targets
[?2004l[?2004h> - Enforce key-based authentication (`PasswordAuthentication no`) and disable direct root login (`PermitRootLogin no`) in `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Restrict MySQL binding in `/disk/etc/my.cnf` to `127.0.0.1` and revoke remote root access grants.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Remove unapproved sudoers overrides in `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
