[?2004lh[?2004h> | # | Action | Target | Status | Note & Forensic Evidence Citation |
[?2004l.json`).
2. **MySQL Hardening**: Edit `/[?2004h> |---|--------|--------|--------|-----------------------------------|
[?2004l[?2004h> | 1 | Block inbound threat actor IP | `198.51.100.78` | Proposed | **CORRECTED**: Replaced stale IP `203.0.113.9` with verified attacker origin IP `198.51.100.78` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 2 | Patch BlueKeep (CVE-2019-0708) | N/A (REJECTED) | Cancelled | **REJECTED**: BlueKeep targets Windows RDP; invalid on Linux (`/disk/etc/os-release`, `/sas/vulns.json`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 3 | Neutralize Cron persistence | `/var/spool/cron/root` | OPEN | **DOWNGRADED**: Changed status from `DONE` (unverified) to `OPEN`. Quarantine `/var/spool/cron/root` and strip malicious re-dropper (`/disk/var/spool/cron/root`, `/sas/alerts.json`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 4 | Clean Shell-Init persistence | `/root/.bashrc` | Proposed | **ADDED**: Quarantine `/root/.bashrc` and remove `PROMPT_COMMAND` beaconing to `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/root/.bashrc`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 5 | Remove Sudoers backdoor | `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` | Proposed | **ADDED**: Move `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` to quarantine (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 6 | Disable Systemd service persistence | `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` | Proposed | **ADDED**: Stop/disable service and move service file to quarantine (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`, `/sas/alerts.json`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 7 | Quarantine Miner binary & process | `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | Proposed | **ADDED**: Kill PID and quarantine `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` to `/var/quarantine/` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 8 | Apply SSH Baseline Hardening | `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` | Proposed | **ADDED**: Set `PermitRootLogin no`, `PasswordAuthentication no`, `MaxAuthTries 3` (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, `/sas/baseline.json`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 9 | Apply MySQL Baseline Hardening | `/etc/my.cnf` | Proposed | **ADDED**: Set `bind-address = 127.0.0.1` and revoke remote root privileges (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`, `/sas/baseline.json`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 10 | Rotate Credentials & Internal Pivot Audit | System Accounts / Internal Subnet | Proposed | **ADDED**: Force root/user password rotation, revoke existing SSH keys, and audit internal targets hit by hydra (`/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Prioritized Remediation Steps
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 1: Containment & Quarantine
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Network Containment**: Block `198.51.100.78` at perimeter firewall (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). Block outbound TCP traffic to pool `xmr.ssh.evil:3333` and domain `update-ssh.example.cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Directory Setup**: Create quarantine directory `/var/quarantine/` with mode `0700` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Process Termination**: Kill active process `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` (`/sas/alerts.json`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Binary Quarantine**: Move `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` to `/var/quarantine/.xorg.bak` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 2: Persistence Removal
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Cron Remediation**: Backup `/var/spool/cron/root` to `/var/quarantine/root.cron.bak`. Edit `/var/spool/cron/root` to remove the line executing curl/sh re-dropper payload (`/disk/var/spool/cron/root`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Systemd Remediation**: Stop service `system-update-helper.service`. Disable service via `systemctl disable system-update-helper.service`. Move `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` to `/var/quarantine/system-update-helper.service.bak` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`). Reload systemd daemon (`systemctl daemon-reload`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Shell-Init Remediation**: Backup `/root/.bashrc` to `/var/quarantine/root.bashrc.bak`. Remove lines setting `PROMPT_COMMAND` beaconing to `198.51.100.78` (`/disk/root/.bashrc`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Sudo Backdoor Remediation**: Move `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` to `/var/quarantine/devops.sudoers.bak` (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 3: System Baseline Hardening & Credential Hygiene
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **SSH Hardening**: Edit `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` to enforce:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - `PermitRootLogin no`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - `PasswordAuthentication no`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - `MaxAuthTries 3`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Reload SSH service (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, `/sas/baseline.json`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **MySQL Hardening**: Edit `/etc/my.cnf` to restrict `bind-address = 127.0.0.1` and disable remote root access (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`, `/sas/baseline.json`). Reload MySQL service.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Credential Rotation**: Force password change for `root` and `devops` accounts. Revoke and generate new SSH keypairs across all authorized users.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 4: Scope Expansion & Verification
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Pivot Subnet Audit**: Inspect internal IPs scanned by Hydra from `devops` user history (`/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`) for signs of credential brute-force and downstream compromise.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Verification Check**: Execute `crontab -l`, `systemctl list-unit-files`, and inspect `/root/.bashrc` to confirm complete removal of persistent triggers.
